                <h2 id="faqs">8. FAQs — Self Credit Builder for US Users</h2>
                <div class="mt-4 divide-y border rounded-2xl bg-white">
                    <div class="p-5">
                        <h3 class="mt-0 !text-[16px]">Is Self Credit Builder legit and FDIC insured?</h3>
                        <p>Yes. Self's partner Lead Bank is Member FDIC. Your CD is insured up to $250k. Self itself is not a bank, but the CD account is. Self has 1.8M+ US customers and BBB accreditation. Complaints on CFPB portal are mostly about fees — read disclosure.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="p-5">
                        <h3 class="mt-0 !text-[16px]">Can I build credit without SSN using Self?</h3>
                        <p>No. For US credit building, you need SSN or ITIN to report to Experian, Equifax, TransUnion. Self requires SSN for Credit Builder loan. If you have no SSN, you cannot generate a FICO Score in US. Alternatives: ITIN can work for reporting, or start with rent reporting services that accept ITIN.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="p-5">
                        <h3 class="mt-0 !text-[16px]">How fast does Self report?</h3>
                        <p>First report in 30-45 days to all 3 bureaus. Then monthly on statement date if paid 5+ days before. If you miss due date, it's not reported late until 30+ days past due per CFPB rules.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="p-5">
                        <h3 class="mt-0 !text-[16px]">Does Self Visa builder card cost extra?</h3>
                        <p>Self offers a secured Visa with $25 annual fee, separate from loan. The loan itself has $9 admin + interest. You can have loan only, card only, or both. Card reports as secured revolving, loan as installment — best mix is both if you can afford.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="p-5">
                        <h3 class="mt-0 !text-[16px]">What happens if I miss a payment?</h3>
                        <p>Grace period 15 days, late fee $15 after. If 30 days late, Self reports late payment to all 3 bureaus, which can drop score 60-110 points (CFPB). Set autopay — Experian recommends autopay for credit-builder loans specifically.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

